  "notes": [
    "CT-PT-1: 5 to 6 exercises x 3 sets, RIR 2 on compounds, RIR 1 on isolation, RIR 3 on core and carries, each day finishing with a carry or core exercise. A-3's AMRAP Last Set gives way to CT-PT-1's RIR 1 on isolation (G-20: the higher RIR wins).",
    "CT-PT-3: an injury the lifter lists changes only the movements it aggravates. Swap those slots with choices, each with its reason in training terms (for example a box squat for a controlled knee depth).",
    "CT-PT-8: every week is written out with a named progression (double progression, A-6), then an L-7 deload in week 4 (30 to 50% fewer sets, RIR + 1, at least 3).",
    "CT-PT-2: each day opens with the mobility block for its pattern (knee, hinge or upper): 5 min rower or bike, three 1-set drills, then Shoulder Big 3 1 x 15 each.",
    "CT-SEL-8: a lifter without a barbell, rack and bench comes here whatever the primary type; each equipment swap is listed in the draft notes."
  ]
}
